#
# **Read off a run of this task at this tree, which agreed at 127.** The lesson this entry
# earns is sharper than "measure, do not derive": a walk of the INTERMEDIATE commits is
# what shows a retirement to be internal, and a diff of the two ends cannot, because a
# block born and deleted between them is absent from both. This branch's own earlier
# versions of this note said "TWO new rows" for rows that no longer exist, then "NO new
# row" one edit after that, then an arithmetic landing one short. All three were written
# while the tree was still moving, which is exactly what a carried figure is.
#
# 127 → the figure below, and this one moved for a reason NO previous entry had: the
# WALK widened rather than the tree gaining a record. `scripts/*.sh` and `.githooks/*`
# joined the population, contributing FIVE harness blocks — two in
